horizon zero dawn is truly enormous  which if you've got the 40 hours to  spare is kind of an awesome thing given  its quite the undertaking though here's  a few things to keep in mind that should  help you out as you venture through the  post post-apocalyptic world  first up there are a hell of a lot of  things you can pick up and your  inventory is limited but you can craft  bigger carrying pouches for your various  item types if you're wondering which of  the many pack upgrades you should craft  I would seriously recommend getting your  resources pack as large as possible as  quickly as possible so check out what  items you need to collect to do so and  try to grab them give everything an  initial bump but beyond that you'll  likely be selling crap equipment mods or  swapping out your weapons for better  ones so you don't need the extra slots  on the other hand almost every resource  is a crafting item or a trading item and  you won't want to get rid of any just in  case you need that raccoon skin or watch  your learns later on pick up icons turn  red when you can't collect any more of  an item but things like branches are  unlimited so if you find yourself  carrying around 500 of them you might  want to drop some and make room for  other items in terms of exploration hit  all the campfires you come across apart  from being good save points they also  serve as fast travel points for when you  inevitably need to backtrack across the  continent for something fast travel  requires using consumable travel packs  but there is an item that lets you fast  travel unlimited times you should pick  this up from a merchant as soon as it's  available if you aren't a fan of walking  if you can't find it it's down the  bottom of their resources tab you can  and should buy treasure maps pretty  early on that will give you the  locations of different collectables  which you can trade in for treasure  boxes generally binoculars are found  high on mountains colored with bright  tribal markings to help you see where  the climber bulerías are metal flowers  are huge blossoms encircled in a ring of  nonmetal flowers and ancient vessels aka  mugs can be found in piles of ancient  debris both will come up purple when you  get close I'd recommend getting to the  middle of the area where the item is  supposed to be and flicking  you're focused then you'll be looking  for fuzzy purple areas if you're lacking  in loot grab extra loot perks in  scavenger skill tree early on if you  find that taking out machines for shards  becomes tedious no you'll find a lot  more simply by completing quests and by  raiding supply boxes in bandit camps and  towns your focus can help you find these  easier every merchant also has a free  sample box which you should totally get  you know because it's free in terms of  combat you'll mainly be scanning robots  for weaknesses and adjusting your  arsenal accordingly if you like playing  it sneaky you can perform stealth  takedowns from the relative safety of a  bush over and over and over again with  the laws skill result death pit it takes  some time but it's great fun the rest of  combat is really balancing and comboing  your skills with one another whether  that be a dodge knockdown and critical  hit with your spear or a time slowdown  concentrated precision shot with your  bow from the air every time you get a  new weapon you'll also get a tutorial  quest where using it in a certain way  will grant you a significant amount of  experience the problem with this is you  have to make sure the tutorial mission  is activated in order for it to register  yes  it's very annoying but now you know  there's obviously way more to learn but  hopefully these tips will alleviate a  few annoyances for all our upcoming  horizon content be sure to subscribe and  check back to GameSpot  you  [Music]
 

